 | `Cadence.keyBeat` | the walking keys | One to two ticks of no keys between one direction and its opposite. |
-| `Cadence.hotbarSwitch` | every change of the held item (`utils/HotbarSwitch.java`, `InventoryBehavior#hold`) | Two to five ticks between deciding on a slot - the best tool for a block, a block to throw down, the builder's next material - and pressing its key, during which neither mouse button is pressed: the click comes after the item is in the hand, never before, and a right click with the wrong item in hand is a bucket emptied. The beat before the click runs underneath, so a switch costs its own beat and no more. A mind changed while the beat runs presses the last key decided on when it is up, rather than starting over, so two callers taking turns cannot stop the hand. The water bucket under a fall is the one item still grabbed on the tick: it is a reflex with a deadline. |
